# tb_pc9821_rhythm_probe - measurement log (not a gate; see the bench header)
# Run: verilator --binary --timing ... --top-module tb_pc9821_rhythm_probe over every source in
# src/opna/opna.qip + src/pc9821/common/pc9821_dpram.sv + the bench, 50 MHz.
# Stimulus: all-zero ROM image (a pure +2/nibble ramp), all six drums keyed at full level.
#
NOTE rhythm_probe: 53518 cen6 slots dumped to rhythm_cen.txt   (80 ms; 666 kHz slots)

# Analysis of rhythm_cen.txt (the drum bus = jt08_adpcm_acc.u_acc_left.pcm_out;
# the pre-CDC node = jt08_acc.u_left.snd):

## 1. Early window (the first 3000 cen6 = 4.5 ms, every drum still ramping, NO overload yet)
bus updates (distinct values)   = 75, one per 36 cen6 = 18.5 kHz, perfectly periodic
largest |step| between updates  = 96 LSB   (six drums x +15 LSB per round)
falling (negative) steps        = 0 of 74
=> the six-drum round-robin (skip/gate/half) drops no round, doubles no round, and the
   sum is glitch-free with all six drums at once. AUDIO_AUDIT.md RP-2.

## 2. Full 80 ms run
cen6 slots dumped               = 53518
drum-bus updates                = 1478
largest step                    = +11552
most negative step              = -30688
The only steps of that size are (a) the authentic 12-bit overload wrap on the drums whose
0x00-image ramps pass 1024 nibbles (the snare/cymbal/tom/rim), i.e. -4096 acc -> -30720 out
(AUDIO_AUDIT.md RP-1), and (b) each drum's end-of-sample cut, which for this image is large BY
CONSTRUCTION (a +2/nibble ramp never decays). The image is deliberately non-decaying, so its
tail cuts are not a property of a real drum.

## 3. The pre-CDC node (jt08_acc.u_left.snd, the FM+ADPCM accumulator)
FM+ADPCM updates                = 1479 (one per drum-bus update, the FM being silent here)
values that are not the drum bus at their own cen6 = 1 (cen 13, the power-up transient)
=> the drum term is added exactly once per FM sample period at the cen_pcm_a slot and no
   sample is added twice or dropped. AUDIO_AUDIT.md RP-5.

## 4. Decode differential against ymfm (offline, same image, ymfm adpcm_a_channel arithmetic)
dec[k] == model[nibble_address(k) - 1] at every sampled drum tick (the -1 is the decoder's own
constant one-nibble pipeline offset); drum bus  == ((acc*15)>>1) & ~3 (measured ratio 7.5 = the
max level the probe programs), which is ymfm's ((int16(acc<<4)*mul)>>shift) & ~3 with mul=15,
shift=5. Address sequence: one nibble per 36 cen6, high nibble first, stopping at the end
byte's second nibble (0x037F for the bass drum, end = 0x01BF) - never end+1.
=> AUDIO_AUDIT.md RP-2.
